<usx version="3.1">
<book code="3JN" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">3 John</para>

<para style="toc1">3 John</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="3JN 1"/>

<para style="s">A Greeting from the Elder</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="3JN 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 John 1:1–3</char></note>The elder, </para>

<para style="p" vid="3JN 1:1">To Gaius the beloved, whom I love in truth. <verse eid="3JN 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="3JN 1:2"/>Beloved, concerning all things I pray you to prosper and to be in good health, just as your soul prospers. <verse eid="3JN 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="3JN 1:3"/>For I rejoiced exceedingly <char style="add">on</char> the brothers' coming and testifying of your truth, just as you are walking in truth. <verse eid="3JN 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="3JN 1:4"/>I have no greater joy<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">grace</char></note> than these things, that I should hear of my children walking in the truth.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in truth</char></note> <verse eid="3JN 1:4"/></para>

<para style="s">Gaius Commended for Hospitality</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="3JN 1:5"/>Beloved, you are doing faithfully whatever you might work for the brothers, and they are strangers,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and for those who are strangers</char></note> <verse eid="3JN 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="3JN 1:6"/>who testified of your love before the church, whom you will do well having sent forward worthily of God. <verse eid="3JN 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="3JN 1:7"/>For they went out on behalf of the Name,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Scrivener TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His name</char></note> receiving nothing from the Gentiles. <verse eid="3JN 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="3JN 1:8"/>Therefore we ought to support<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to receive</char></note> such, so that we may be fellow workers in the truth. <verse eid="3JN 1:8"/></para>

<para style="s">Diotrephes and Demetrius</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="3JN 1:9"/>I did write something to the church; but the one loving to be first among them, Diotrephes, does not welcome us. <verse eid="3JN 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="3JN 1:10"/>Because of this, if I should come, I will bring to remembrance his works that he is doing, prattling against us with evil words; and not being satisfied with these, neither does he welcome the brothers himself, and he forbids those intending, and he casts <char style="add">them</char> out of the church. <verse eid="3JN 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="3JN 1:11"/>Beloved, do not imitate what <char style="add">is</char> evil, but what <char style="add">is</char> good. The one doing good is of God; the one doing evil has not seen God. <verse eid="3JN 1:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="3JN 1:12"/>Testimony has been given to Demetrius by all, and by the truth itself; and we also testify, and you know<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">we know</char></note> that our testimony is true. <verse eid="3JN 1:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Conclusion2 John 1:12–13</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="3JN 1:13"/>I had many things to write to you,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to you</char></note> but I do not want to write to you with ink and pen; <verse eid="3JN 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="3JN 1:14"/>but I hope to see you soon, and we will speak mouth to mouth.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and speak with you face to face</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; some translators begin a new verse (15) after </char><char style="fq" closed="false">mouth to mouth.</char></note> </para>

<para style="p" vid="3JN 1:14">Peace to you. </para>

<para style="p" vid="3JN 1:14">The friends greet you. </para>

<para style="p" vid="3JN 1:14">Greet the friends by name. <verse eid="3JN 1:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="3JN 1"/>

</usx>
